# No rustc/cargo build-dependency is declared on purpose. tpmd declares
# rust-version = "1.98" and uses edition 2024, which is newer than the rustc in
# every currently supported Debian-like release, so the build dependency could
# not be satisfied anywhere. The toolchain is supplied by the build environment
# instead; see debian/rules and docs/install.md for what that means and what
# would have to change for a package built in the archive.

Package: tpmd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: local key agent that signs on behalf of local applications
 tpmd owns private signing keys and signs on behalf of local applications over
 a local socket, so that a consumer never sees key material: it asks for a
 signature and gets one, or gets a refusal that says why.
 .
 Keys live at a security level — file, keyring, sealed or hardware — and the
 daemon selects the strongest level the machine can actually reach. It refuses
 to serve anything below the floor it was started with rather than quietly
 handing out a weaker key, it never re-keys a device to satisfy a request, and
 it never replaces a lost key with a weaker one.
 .
 This package installs the system-wide agent: a socket-activated service that
 serves every local user and authorises each caller from kernel peer
 credentials. A per-user agent can also be run by hand, and the tpmd-demo tool
 shipped here exercises an installed agent end to end.
